From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t31: replace stale flat sensor proc symlinks

When a tx-isp instance leaves /proc/jz/sensor behind, the next
publish calls proc_symlink() for an entry that already exists and
procfs warns "already registered". Remove the stale entry first.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
diff --git a/driver/common/tx_isp_sinfo.c b/driver/common/tx_isp_sinfo.c
index f1d33719..cd5ecfe1 100644
--- a/driver/common/tx_isp_sinfo.c
+++ b/driver/common/tx_isp_sinfo.c
@@ -922,6 +922,13 @@ static void tx_isp_sinfo_flat_publish(void)
 			continue;
 		snprintf(target, sizeof(target), "sensor0/%s",
 			 tx_isp_sinfo_key_name[key]);
+		/*
+		 * A previous tx-isp instance can leave the flat symlink behind
+		 * when its proc root was torn down separately. Replacing it
+		 * avoids the proc_dir_entry already registered warning.
+		 */
+		remove_proc_entry(tx_isp_sinfo_key_name[key],
+				  tx_isp_sinfo_root);
 		proc_symlink(tx_isp_sinfo_key_name[key], tx_isp_sinfo_root,
 			     target);
 	}
